    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01HDEF752Z80X46FDXNFR7B9Y1\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to enable collision prevention display settings to prevent multiple sign-up forms from appearing simultaneously or one after another for your shoppers. If you have multiple sign-up forms live on your website, and each with its own rule-based display triggers, enable collision prevention to ensure that the forms won’t overlap and overwhelm your site visitors.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HDEF752ZNSSNM2HG5Z4Y6B8F\">Enable collision prevention</h2>\n<p>You only need to enable collision-prevention 1 time in your form display settings, and it will apply across all pages on your website once set. </p>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>Note that enabling form collision settings will only block collisions between popup, flyout, and full page sign-up forms. Embedded forms and custom-triggered forms will not be impacted by collision prevention display settings. </p>\n</div>\n<p>To enable collision prevention:</p>\n<ol>\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to the <strong>Sign-up forms</strong> tab. </li>\n<li>Select the gear icon in the top right corner. <br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28716356571291\" alt=\"The gear icon to select in the top corner of the Sign-up forms tab that will open the form display settings menu.\">\n</li>\n<li>On the form settings modal that appears, check the box next to <em>Don’t show multiple forms at the same time.</em>\n</li>\n<li>From here, choose from further display settings:\n<ul>\n<li><em><em>Show only one form per session</em></em></li>\n<li><em>Show next form after a time delay (minutes or seconds)<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28716356569371\" alt=\"The form settings modal with Don't show multiple forms at the same time selected and Show next form after a 5 second time delay selected. \"></em></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Moving forward, your elected collision prevention display settings will prevent multiple sign-up forms from showing at the same time or in rapid succession. Keep in mind that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>Form teasers may not show</strong><br>If <em>Form display</em> settings are set to <em>Show only one form per session</em>, <a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4411540984859\">form teasers</a> won't appear on your site, since they are considered another form showing in the same visit. If you want teasers to appear after someone closes a form, use a time delay (e.g., set a 5-minute time delay to show the teaser 5 minutes after the form is closed.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Form order can't be configured<br></strong><em>Form display settings</em> do not allow you to configure the order in which 2 sign-up forms with the same trigger settings will display. You can configure which sign-up forms appear when by adjusting a form's trigger settings in the <strong><a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4413544555547\">Targeting &amp; behaviors</a></strong> tab of the form editor. If you have 2 sign-up forms with the exact same trigger settings, these forms will show in alphabetical order according to their Form ID (e.g., A12345 will show before B1234 if they have the same trigger settings). The form ID is the 6-digit code at the end of the URL in the form editor.<br><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28716356577947\" alt=\"The Form Id highlighted in the form editor URL for an example sign-up form.\">\n</li>\n<li>\n<strong>Frequency settings may be impacted by form display settings</strong><br>If you configure your display settings to <em>Show only one form per session</em>, each visitor will only see the first form they're eligible for during their visit one time, even if it's set to display again right away <em>(0 days after opening</em>).  </li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HDEF75302JJE7AHFH3ZDEMHY\">Additional resources</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4413544555547\">Understanding targeting and behavior for sign-up forms</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360002049952\">How to manage your sign-up forms</a></li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/14980194112411\">How to create ADA-friendly sign-up forms</a> </li>\n</ul>",
    "user_segment_ids": []
  },
